# AGENTS.md — Grok Build + AIWG

This project uses AIWG with the experimental `grok-build` provider.

## Discover AIWG capabilities

```bash
export PATH="$(npm prefix -g)/bin:$PATH"
aiwg discover "<need>"
aiwg show skill <name>
```

Grok Build does not claim that the host auto-loads the full AIWG corpus. Prefer
explicit `aiwg discover` / `aiwg show` for framework artifacts.

## Native paths

- Project skills: `.grok/skills/`
- Project agents: `.grok/agents/`
- Project rules/hooks/config: `.grok/rules/`, `.grok/hooks/`, `.grok/config.toml`
- User home: `$GROK_HOME` (default `~/.grok`) — skills under `$GROK_HOME/skills/`

This bridge is distinct from Grok Bot (`grokbot` / `AIWG_GROKBOT_SKILLS_DIR`).
